# Re-entry regression (style-leak class): enter -> exit -> re-enter.
# The second entry re-runs app_init -> game_snake_gui_init; re-running
# lv_style_init() on a static style leaks its property array. Under
# LV_USE_ASSERT_STYLE, LVGL logs "Potential memory leak" and the runner
# fails the scenario on any such warning. The screenshot has no golden
# on purpose — it is uploaded as a candidate artifact.
# (snake historically avoided the re-entry leak via lv_style_reset in
# game_snake_gui_del; this scenario pins the once-guard idiom instead.)

app snake

wait_ms 400
assert_no_crash

action RETURN
wait_ms 200

action GO_FORWORD
wait_ms 400
screenshot 01_reentry
assert_no_crash

action RETURN
wait_ms 200
assert_no_crash
